  "instance_name": "juxtaposition_meme_structure",
  "label": "Juxtaposition Meme Structure",
  "description": "The meme uses a juxtaposition structure: a serious or culturally specific image (three men in a savanna) paired with an absurd or incongruous question ('when did you have lunch?'). This structure is common in internet memes to create humor through contrast, but in this case, the contrast is built on a reductive and potentially offensive stereotype about the subjects' daily lives and capabilities.",
